{
	if (bpf_res_spin_lock(&lock_a))
		return 0;
	if (bpf_res_spin_lock(&lock_b)) {
		bpf_res_spin_unlock(&lock_a);
		return 0;
	}
	// Fix: unlock lock_b first, then lock_a
	bpf_res_spin_unlock(&lock_b);
	bpf_res_spin_unlock(&lock_a);
	return 0;
}
```

This should resolve the verifier error.

Note: The verifier log we saw was from the non-error path (both locks acquired) and it was failing because we tried to unlock lock_a while lock_b was still held. The fix corrects the order.

